  "result": "Perfect! All 95 tests pass (6 new tests for ID normalization). Here's a summary of the implementation:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Features Added:\n1. **`normalizeId()` function** - Trims whitespace and converts to uppercase for consistent handling\n2. **Automatic normalization in `getCustomer()`** - Accepts mixed case and spaces when looking up customers\n3. **Storage normalization in `createInvoice()`** - Stores the normalized customer ID on the invoice\n\n### Function Signature:\n```javascript\nnormalizeId(id) \u2192 uppercase and trimmed string\n```\n\n### Examples:\n- `'c-001'` \u2192 `'C-001'`\n- `' c-007 '` \u2192 `'C-007'`\n- `'C-001'` \u2192 `'C-001'`\n- `' C-007 '` \u2192 `'C-007'`\n\n### Changes Made:\n- **src/customers.js**:\n  - Added `normalizeId()` export that trims and uppercases IDs\n  - Updated `getCustomer()` to normalize the input ID before lookup\n- **src/invoices.js**:\n  - Imported `normalizeId` from customers\n  - Updated `createInvoice()` to normalize and store the customer ID\n- **test/customers.test.js**: \n  - Imported `normalizeId`\n  - Added 4 new tests for `normalizeId()` function\n  - Added 1 new test for `getCustomer()` with mixed case IDs\n- **test/invoices.test.js**:\n  - Added 2 new tests for `createInvoice()` with mixed case IDs\n\n### Test Results:\n\u2705 All 95 tests pass (6 new tests for ID normalization)\n\nThe system now robustly handles customer IDs from external systems regardless of case or whitespace, while always storing and comparing them in normalized form.",
